From b5e7c2638a9b7a5cc30d16e5abb2b73dba2eec69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yangsonglin13 <yangsonglin566@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:18:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(rfork): configurable seed server ports and
 TransferEngine port-0 binding

- Add seed_port_base config (default 0 = OS-assigned); each rank reserves
  adjacent main/draft seed HTTP port slots (base + 2 * global_rank + slot)
  with fallback to OS assignment when the port is occupied or exceeds 65535.
  The value is passed through to __post_init__ so a misspelled type (for
  example a string port) fails fast instead of silently falling back to
  dynamic ports, matching the other numeric config fields.
- Initialize YuanRong TransferEngine with host:0 and read back the actual
  port via get_rpc_port(), removing the get_open_port() check-then-bind
  race; the resolved endpoint is validated and published as the transfer
  session id. If get_rpc_port() itself raises, the initialized engine is
  finalized before propagating the error so native RPC threads and the
  bound port never leak.
- Streamline unit test coverage: consolidate repetitive compatibility
  matrices into focused test loops and remove implementation-only
  assertions. Keep explicit 408/429 retryable-classification cases for
  lease release and seed report: they hit the explicit tuple branch in
  the planner response classification, which the retained 503 cases (5xx
  range branch) cannot cover.
- Document YuanRong's YR_TE_RPC_PORT_MIN/MAX range env vars and note that
  HIXL data-plane endpoints default to base port 22000, clear of Mooncake
  ADXL's default 20000-based segments.

Signed-off-by: yangsonglin13 <yangsonglin566@gmail.com>
